{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/group(_:)"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keeps the given component types packed in the same order, so that queries and updates of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly these types visit their entities without lookups."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"group","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"types","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": repeat (each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":").Type) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" repeat each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Component","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule9ComponentP","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Component"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"types","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The component types to keep packed together.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A query of several types normally walks one type’s storage and looks up the entity in each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the others. After you group the types, the entities that hold all of them sit at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"front of each type’s storage, at the same positions, and spawning, inserting, removing and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"despawning keep them there. A query of the same types in any order, or an update that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes and reads exactly those types, walks that front directly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use a group for a set of types you visit together on every step, such as position and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"velocity:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","let comet = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","world.spawn(Position(x: 9, y: 9))","world.group(Position.self, Velocity.self)","","world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","    position.x += row.components.dx","    position.y += row.components.dy","}","print(world[Position.self, of: comet])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Grouping doesn’t change which entities a query or update visits, only how it finds them."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It does change the order queries list entities in, and makes adding and removing the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grouped types a little slower. Each type belongs to at most one group. A copy of the world"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps the group; a snapshot doesn’t."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"·"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" entities in the smallest of the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" types."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"types","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists at least two distinct types, and no other group owns any of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them. The checked spelling, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/group(checked:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", throws instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"WorldModule","title":"group(_:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"group","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(repeat (each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":").Type)","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Group.swift#L70","fileName":"Group.swift"},"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"externalID":"s:11WorldModule0A0V5groupyyxmxQpRvzAA9ComponentRzlF"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/group(_:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Speeding Up Queries","anchor":"Speeding-Up-Queries","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/group(checked:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/cache(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/index(_:)-u1gw","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/index(_:)-2gtfg","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/lookup(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModul